# Spec-Driven Generation

For boilerplate-heavy patterns, provide high-level spec formats that AI generates implementation from.

## Core Principle

SpecGeneration {
  IdentifyBoilerplate => find repetitive patterns that are typical in develpment while using stack
  DefineSpec => create concise format for each pattern
  GenerateImplementation => AI produces full code from spec
  MakeDiscoverable => user can find available specs via /help
}

## Per-Stack Patterns

When generating stack rules, identify what can be spec-driven:

CommonPatterns {
  StateManagement => slice/store specs → actions, reducers, selectors
  Components => component specs → full component with props, state, handlers
  API => endpoint specs → handlers, validation, types
  Database => model specs → schema, queries, migrations
  Forms => form specs → validation, fields, submission
}

## Spec Format

Specs should be:
- Concise (SudoLang or similar high-level format)
- Complete (contain all info needed to generate)
- Readable (understandable without knowing implementation)

SpecStructure {
  Name => identifier
  Shape => data structure / types
  Behaviors => what it does
  Constraints => rules it must follow
}

## Discovery

Generated command systems should include:

DiscoveryRules {
  /help => lists available spec types for this stack
  /[pattern] => explains spec format, shows minimal example
  /[pattern] --generate => generates implementation from spec
}

## Generation Commands

For each identified pattern, generate a command:

CommandPattern {
  Name => /[pattern-name]
  Input => spec in SudoLang or structured format
  Output => full implementation in target language
  Files => list of files to generate
}

## Lifecycle Calibration

| Aspect | PoC | TeamTool | Production |
|--------|-----|----------|------------|
| Spec patterns | Optional | Key patterns | Comprehensive |
| Generated tests | Skip | Include | Required |
| Generated docs | Skip | Minimal | Full |

Constraints {
  Identify boilerplate patterns for chosen stack.
  Define spec format for each pattern.
  Generate /[pattern] command for each.
  List available patterns in /help output.
  Specs should be shorter than generated output.
}
